283: ## 6. The exact primitive suspension square
284: 
285: Let \(U\) denote the rational target-point lift of translation by
286: \(-G\) on \(O(G-O)\):
287: \[
288:                  (p,w)\longmapsto
289:                  \left(p-G,\frac{w}{X(p-G)}\right).          \tag{SZ.7}
290: \]
291: The divisor identity making this a line map is
292: \[
293:  (G)-O-t_G^*((G)-O)=(G)+(-G)-2O=\operatorname{div}X
294: \]
295: on each ordinary elliptic fibre. The displayed factor is evaluated
296: at the target point. This convention is the same convention as the
297: actual coefficient \(\phi=q/(vF_{12})\) in Section 3.
298: 
299: For a point \(r=(X,Y)\) on the source curve, the addition formula gives
300: \[
301:  X(r+G)=\left(\frac{Y-v}{X}\right)^2-(1-2v)-X,
302: \]
303: and the source equation then gives the exact identity
304: \[
305:                          X(r+G)X(r)=-2vF_{12}(r).            \tag{SZ.8}
306: \]
307: Therefore the suspension in the \((a,b)=(1,2)\) family is
308: \[
309:                     B_\lambda=-2\lambda q\,U^2.             \tag{SZ.9}
310: \]
311: This is an equality of actual rational line maps, not just of their
312: generic Picard points. It retains the scalar and the selected
313: whole-fibre factor.
314: 
315: The local nonzero line above the exceptional source component also
316: has a literal Cox presentation. Write
317: \[
318:  D=s_0t_0,\quad A=s_1t_0,\quad B=s_0t_1,\quad C=s_1t_1,
319: \]
320: where the auxiliary action has weights \((1,1,-1,-1)\). Since
321: \(O(G-O)|_{C_1}=O(1)\), the nonzero line coordinate has auxiliary
322: weight \(+1\). Fixing it to one leaves the actual coordinates
323: \[
324:   (s_0,s_1,t_0,t_1),\qquad (s_0,s_1)\ne(0,0),\qquad
325:                    v=\frac{s_0t_1-s_1t_0}{2}.               \tag{SZ.10}
326: \]
327: The Hessian determinant of this quadratic is \(1/16\), so this map
328: is explicitly nondegenerate. The physical delta action is retained:
329: it has weights \((-1,-1,+1,+1)\) after this gauge choice. For the
330: degree-two line the same gauge has the residual \(\mu_2\) action;
331: it must not be discarded.
332: 
333: Equations (SZ.7)--(SZ.10) identify the component exchange whose graph
334: must be resolved. They do not yet identify the quotient of its
335: relative completion with the original compact family: \(U\) has
336: component poles, and its chosen source model changes by a flop at
337: the central curve. A generic translation logarithm across \(v=0\)
338: has therefore not been used.
339: 
340: ## 7. Finite-root units and the remaining comparison
341: 
342: The source-parameter pole of the selected Hom coefficient is not a
343: pole of every cap coefficient. For the good III* root of the
344: \((a,b)=(1,2)\) case, put \(T=z^{-4},X=z^{-2}X',Y=z^{-3}Y'\).
345: Then literal substitution in (SZ.1) gives
346: \[
347:  \phi_{12}=
348:  \frac{1-(v^2-2v)z^4}
349:  {-1/2+vz^3Y'/X'-v^2z^6/X'}.
350:                                                                \tag{SZ.11}
351: \]
352: Its generic central-component value is \(-2\), with no winding in
353: \(v\). For a reduced III root \(m=4p-1\) in the \((a,b)=(2,1)\)
354: case, the analogous substitution gives
355: \[
356:  \phi_{21}=
357:  \frac{1-(v^2-2v)z^m}
358:  {1/2+vz^{m-p}Y'/X'+v^2z^{m+2p}/X'}.
359:                                                                \tag{SZ.12}
360: \]
361: The generic central-component value is \(+2\). The certificate checks
362: the good root and the basic reduced root literally. Extension through
363: all resolved root components still belongs to the required completed
364: family comparison; the generic values alone do not supply it.
365: 
366: The present exact remaining map is the relative graph completion of
367: the suspension (SZ.9), or its degree-two-line counterpart, through
368: the central flop, with the chosen finite-root line maps and physical
369: delta kept. Rescaling \(\lambda=v^2\lambda_0\) cancels the selected
370: Hom-unit pole, but changes the actual scalar loop by two turns.
371: The scalar-loop contribution and every cap gluing must consequently
372: be retained in any argument using that rescaling. No numerical
373: source-loop return follows merely from the signature of the blown-up
374: normalization or from (SZ.6).
375: 
376: All displayed algebraic identities in Sections 5--7 are checked in
377: code/part3_fourfold/source_zero_trace.py, with JSON and captured
378: outputs. Its status explicitly stops at the source, Cartier and
379: suspension identities.
